notes:
From the 30-session retro (2026-11-16). The manager gets flooded with worker notices and polls on every one:
- "finished its turn": 44 in a dotfiles manager session, 42 in openwrt-config.
- "stopped without sending you a report": 25 in a new-crm manager session, and 12 for a pane the user was talking to directly.
- One new-crm manager read worker session logs by hand 62 times to learn what a worker was doing.

The cause: notices fire while the worker's background /pr-loop, CI wait or /simplify agents are still running.

Want:
- one notice per turn, only when the Stop hook input shows no background tasks or wakeups left;
- the notice carries the worker's last assistant message, or a short tail of it;
- no notice when the pane's last prompt came from the user rather than the manager;
- `pane report <id>` prints a worker's state and last message, so the manager never greps ~/.claude/projects.
